{
  "format": "bench-library",
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "ps2-controller",
  "name": "PS2 wireless controller",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "author": "Bench Workshop",
  "owner": "codeopen0-cpu",
  "description": "The PS2-style wireless game pad that comes with most robot car kits: its receiver goes on the board (PS2X_lib.h), the pad's buttons and sticks drive the robot. Play it with a real game pad plugged into your PC, the keyboard (arrows, 1-4, Q/E, Enter), or the run panel.",
  "category": "Controls",
  "needsApp": "0.9.0",
  "code": "device.js",
  "sketch": {
    "PS2X_lib.h": { "classes": ["PS2X"], "exports": ["PSB_SELECT", "PSB_L3", "PSB_R3", "PSB_START", "PSB_PAD_UP", "PSB_PAD_RIGHT", "PSB_PAD_DOWN", "PSB_PAD_LEFT", "PSB_L2", "PSB_R2", "PSB_L1", "PSB_R1", "PSB_GREEN", "PSB_RED", "PSB_BLUE", "PSB_PINK", "PSB_TRIANGLE", "PSB_CIRCLE", "PSB_CROSS", "PSB_SQUARE", "PSS_RX", "PSS_RY", "PSS_LX", "PSS_LY", "PSAB_PAD_RIGHT", "PSAB_PAD_UP", "PSAB_PAD_DOWN", "PSAB_PAD_LEFT", "PSAB_L2", "PSAB_R2", "PSAB_L1", "PSAB_R1", "PSAB_GREEN", "PSAB_RED", "PSAB_BLUE", "PSAB_PINK", "PSAB_TRIANGLE", "PSAB_CIRCLE", "PSAB_CROSS", "PSAB_SQUARE"], "file": "sketch/PS2X_lib.js" }
  },
  "parts": [
    {
      "id": "ps2-receiver",
      "name": "PS2 controller receiver",
      "description": "The wireless pad's receiver: wire DAT, CMD, ATT (also called CS / SEL) and CLK to four pins, VCC to 3.3 V (5 V on many boards' receivers works too) and GND. With #include <PS2X_lib.h>: PS2X ps2x; ps2x.config_gamepad(CLK, CMD, ATT, DAT, false, false) == 0 when it finds the pad; in loop(): ps2x.read_gamepad(); ps2x.Button(PSB_PAD_UP), ps2x.ButtonPressed(PSB_CROSS), ps2x.Analog(PSS_LY) (0 up .. 128 middle .. 255 down). The pad: a game pad on your PC, the keyboard (arrows = D-pad, 1-4 = triangle circle cross square, Q / E = L1 / R1, Enter = Start), or the run panel.",
      "swatch": "#1a1a1c", "mass": 8,
      "shape": [
        { "box": [3.2, 1.2, 2.2], "at": [0, 0.6, 0], "color": "#1a1a1c" },
        { "screen": { "id": "led", "size": [0.3, 0.3], "px": [1, 1], "mode": "pixels", "on": "#30d158", "off": "#123018", "bg": "#1a1a1c" }, "at": [0.9, 1.21, 0.5] }
      ],
      "pins": [
        { "id": "DAT", "label": "DAT (data from the pad)", "at": [-1.3, 0.3, -1.15], "kind": "out" },
        { "id": "CMD", "label": "CMD (commands to it)", "at": [-0.9, 0.3, -1.15], "kind": "in" },
        { "id": "VCC", "label": "VCC (3.3 V)", "at": [-0.5, 0.3, -1.15], "kind": "vin", "vmin": 3.0, "vmax": 5.5 },
        { "id": "GND", "at": [-0.1, 0.3, -1.15], "kind": "gnd" },
        { "id": "ATT", "label": "ATT (CS / SEL)", "at": [0.3, 0.3, -1.15], "kind": "in" },
        { "id": "CLK", "label": "CLK", "at": [0.7, 0.3, -1.15], "kind": "in" }
      ],
      "controls": [
        { "id": "on", "kind": "switch", "label": "Pad switched on", "value": true },
        { "id": "buttons", "kind": "keys", "label": "Buttons", "cols": 4, "keys": ["Up", "Down", "Left", "Right", "Triangle", "Circle", "Cross", "Square", "L1", "R1", "L2", "R2", "Start", "Select", "L3", "R3"] },
        { "id": "lx", "kind": "slider", "label": "Left stick left-right", "min": 0, "max": 255, "step": 1, "value": 128 },
        { "id": "ly", "kind": "slider", "label": "Left stick up-down", "min": 0, "max": 255, "step": 1, "value": 128 },
        { "id": "rx", "kind": "slider", "label": "Right stick left-right", "min": 0, "max": 255, "step": 1, "value": 128 },
        { "id": "ry", "kind": "slider", "label": "Right stick up-down", "min": 0, "max": 255, "step": 1, "value": 128 }
      ],
      "device": "ps2"
    }
  ],
  "examples": []
}
